  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GAC Integrated Humanitarian Response to conflict-affected communities in White Nile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the escalating humanitarian crisis in Sudan, the Government of Canada is supporting CAFOD and NCA to deliver life-saving assistance to vulnerable populations affected by conflict, displacement, and protection risks. This project is a consortium between CAFOD and NCA, with each organization leading interventions in different regions of the country. CAFOD is operating in White Nile State through its national partner, Caritas-Sudan, focusing on protection activities targeting internally displaced persons (IDPs), refugees, and host communities. The intervention addresses urgent needs arising from large-scale displacement, gender-based violence, child protection concerns, and lack of access to safe spaces and psychosocial support, particularly for women, girls, and persons with disabilities. By working through local actors, the project aims to protect lives, restore dignity, and promote inclusive recovery for conflict-affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
